    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and fits this codebase's established conventions:\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** `generateCustomerCode` still owns code *construction* (region + hash) and delegates the orthogonal concern of collision resolution to a dedicated private `deduplicateCustomerCode` helper. That's a natural single-responsibility split at the right altitude, not a forced extraction.\n- **Idiomatic for this class.** The `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()...filter(...).collect(...)` approach exactly matches the surrounding pattern used by `isHouseholdInUse`, `isIdentityKeyInUse`, `findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId`, `countNamesakes`, `countOwnersInCity`, and `countOwnersRegisteredOn`. A maintainer of this file would find a repository-wide query method surprising here, whereas the in-memory stream is the house style.\n- **No duplication, no catch-all.** The new helper is self-contained; nothing is copy-pasted, and neither method is becoming a dumping ground. New imports (`Objects`, `Collectors`) are both used.\n- **Documentation kept coherent.** The `generateCustomerCode` Javadoc was extended to describe the new de-dup behavior, and the helper carries its own focused Javadoc consistent with the other private helpers (`hash8`, `normalizeForComparison`).\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
